 infrastructure and APIs"},{"id":1967495446,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxOTY3NDk1NDQ2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch/labels/Team:Core/Infra","name":"Team:Core/Infra","color":"fef2c0","default":false,"description":"Meta label for core/infra team"}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2024-07-12T09:36:51Z","updated_at":"2024-07-26T16:20:29Z","closed_at":"2024-07-26T16:20:29Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Elasticsearch Version\n\n8.14\n\n### Installed Plugins\n\n_No response_\n\n### Java Version\n\n_bundled_\n\n### OS Version\n\nLinux 6.9.7-1-ck-generic-v4\n\n### Problem Description\n\nIn case a `Setting` is defined with a fallback setting and the fallback setting is defined in `elasticsearch.yml`, the response to `_cluster/settings?include_defaults` doesn't return the value defined in `elasticsearch.yml` for the 1st setting. Instead, it returns whatever default is defined for the fallback.\n\n### Steps to Reproduce\n\n- create a setting `my.setting` which defaults to `1`.\r\n- create a setting `my.setting.with_fallback` which falls back to `my.setting`.\r\n- set a value for `my.setting` in `elasticsearch.yml`, e.g., `42`.\r\n- the response of `_cluster/settings?include_defaults` contains `defaults.my.setting.with_fallback: 1`, although what is expected is to get `defaults.my.setting.with_fallback: 42`\n\n### Logs (if relevant)\n\n_No response_","closed_by":{"login":"ldematte","id":2022952,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMjI5NTI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2022952?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ldematte","html_url":"https://github.com/ldematte","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ldematte/followers","fo